.TH EIC\-CURL 1 "2026-10-22" "ec2-instance-connect-rh 0.0.1"
.SH NAME
eic\-curl \- fetch EC2 Instance Connect keys and metadata from IMDS
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B eic\-curl
.I username
.RI [ fingerprint ]
.SH DESCRIPTION
.B eic\-curl
is called by
.BR eic\-run (1).
It communicates with the EC2 Instance Metadata Service (IMDS) to retrieve
an IMDSv2 token, the instance identity, the signer certificate, OCSP
staples, and SSH public keys.
After fetching all data, it invokes
.BR eic\-parse (1)
in\-process to verify and output valid keys.
.PP
The command is not intended to be run interactively.
.SH EXIT CODES
.TP
.B 0
Keys printed to stdout, or soft skip (missing user, non\-EC2 instance).
.TP
.B 1
Certificate or key fetch failure.
.TP
.B 255
IMDS/protocol error.
.SH SEE ALSO
.BR eic\-run (1),
.BR eic\-parse (1),
.BR sshd (8)
